WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.501
-Melanie, Dave,
nice to meet you,

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:05.434
and thank you for
coming on our show.

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:06.734
We appreciate this.

00:00:06.734 --> 00:00:08.667
-Thanks for having us.
-Thanks for having us.

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:10.601
This is awesome.
-I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:13.367
In America.
-Yes, in America. Yes.

00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:16.734
Well, "Bluey" is one of the,
I think, one of the most --

00:00:16.734 --> 00:00:19.067
It's the best show on TV
right now, "Bluey."

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:21.501
I mean, there's "Tonight Show."
-Did you hear that?

00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:23.934
-I did hear that. And who are
your favorite characters?

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:26.367
-Oh, yeah, well, of course
Bandit and Chilli,

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:27.601
of course, my favorite.

00:00:27.601 --> 00:00:29.767
Better than Bluey and Bingo,
of course.

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:33.334
But I think the show is --
It's so funny.

00:00:33.334 --> 00:00:35.067
It's clever.

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:37.367
It's game changing.

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:38.767
I think -- I love it so much.

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:41.334
I've seen more of you guys
and heard more of your voices

00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:43.434
than I've heard my own voice
in my household.

00:00:43.434 --> 00:00:45.634
And the kids aren't even
watching.

00:00:45.634 --> 00:00:47.601
It's just me watching this.
Yeah.

00:00:47.601 --> 00:00:50.467
Melanie, how did you end up
getting the role?

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:54.367
-It was actually quite a
serendipitous situation.

00:00:54.367 --> 00:00:58.667
I was putting a voice-over down
with Joe's brother, Dan,

00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:00.801
who works on the show.

00:01:00.801 --> 00:01:02.234
He plays Stripe.
-And Joe created --

00:01:02.234 --> 00:01:03.667
-Joe created the show.
-Yeah.

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:05.934
-And he said, "My brother's
creating this animation.

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:06.968
You've got a great voice.

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:08.367
Do you want to work some
voice-overs down?

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:10.367
It's already cast, but maybe in
the future."

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:14.434
Anyway so, at the 11th hour, ABC
decided to change up the voices.

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:17.367
I had already seen the pilot,
and I had fallen in love.

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:20.334
Like, the most cute --
Like, my heart hurts.

00:01:20.334 --> 00:01:21.734
This is so cute show.

00:01:21.734 --> 00:01:23.667
So I'm like,
"Yes, use anything."

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:27.100
And then they did their due
diligence and auditioned for

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.501
like three months and then came
back and said,

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:31.033
"No, you were right."

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:33.667
And a year later, the producers
told me that they couldn't find

00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:35.801
the same warmth
from anyone else.

00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:37.267
-Hey. You'll take that.
[ Audience aws ]

00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:39.367
Come on, see. And they were
right. They're correct.

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:41.100
Dave?
-Yeah.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.534
-How did you get this?
-Well --

00:01:42.534 --> 00:01:43.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.901 --> 00:01:47.000
I was walking out of a lift
and someone was walking --

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.834
Someone I knew was walking into
the lift and they said,

00:01:48.834 --> 00:01:52.734
"I know someone who's making a
show about a cartoon dog family.

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:54.601
Maybe you'd want to be
the dad voice?"

00:01:54.601 --> 00:01:58.033
And I was like, "I can't act.
I can't do that."

00:01:58.033 --> 00:01:59.701
And he said, "Can you read?"

00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:01.334
[ Laughter ]
I said, "Well...

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:03.167
I can read a bit."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.167 --> 00:02:06.434
And so they gave me, you know,
a script with highlighted bits

00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:07.868
of where I got to say stuff.

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:10.767
So I started reading
and we just kept going.

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:13.868
And then we sort of had
done a pilot.

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:15.701
And then I thought,
"Oh, this will be nice.

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:17.334
This will be on YouTube
as some sort of,

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:19.801
one-off, you know,
short animation."

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:22.834
And then here we are.
Bigger than the Beatles.

00:02:22.834 --> 00:02:24.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.267 --> 00:02:26.200
-"Bluey" is bigger than
the Beatles, yeah.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.234
And you guys, you were telling
me backstage

00:02:28.234 --> 00:02:30.701
you just met each other --
-Two days ago?

00:02:30.701 --> 00:02:32.434
-Two days ago,
for the first time.

00:02:32.434 --> 00:02:34.534
-So, I'm sorry, how?

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:37.300
-So, we record separately.
-Yeah.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:40.100
-We live in different cities,
and I travel a lot for work.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:42.234
So, this was the first time.

00:02:42.234 --> 00:02:44.467
-How cool is that?
-It was wild. In New York.

00:02:44.467 --> 00:02:46.133
-I know. I thought it would be
all of us sitting

00:02:46.133 --> 00:02:48.367
around a table, you know,
like in the movies when

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:49.801
they're making a TV show.
-Yeah.

00:02:49.801 --> 00:02:51.767
-And everyone is sitting around
the table with coffee

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:54.200
and salads and rolls and stuff.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:57.501
But we're just isolated
in our booths.

00:02:57.501 --> 00:03:00.801
-Yeah.
-You have young kids.

00:03:00.801 --> 00:03:03.501
What do they think of their dad
voicing Bandit?

00:03:03.501 --> 00:03:04.734
-They love it. Rose and Grace.

00:03:04.734 --> 00:03:08.701
They're now --
Grace is almost 9. Rose is 11.

00:03:08.701 --> 00:03:11.901
They love it.
They were confused when it first

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:15.267
came on TV because they'd look
at the TV and Bandit speaking

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:19.133
and look at me and look at the
TV and like, "What's going on?"

00:03:19.133 --> 00:03:20.667
-Yeah, it's so hard to tell
a kid what --

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:23.400
-It's a connection, isn't it?
-Yeah, it's wild.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:26.868
'Cause now when you talk,
all I see is the cartoon.

00:03:26.868 --> 00:03:29.434
-I know. It's weird when parents
say, "Come and meet my kid.

00:03:29.434 --> 00:03:31.467
They love the show."
I'm like, "Oh, don't.

00:03:31.467 --> 00:03:33.000
They normally burst into tears."

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.200
Because they think
I've, like, eaten Bandit

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.467
and his voice is coming out.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:38.901
-They don't understand it, yeah.

00:03:38.901 --> 00:03:41.767
-And they, "Go on, do the
voice." "Hey, how you doing?"

00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:43.200
-But you really just sound
like Bandit.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.067
-"He's doing the voice! Oh, my
God, he's doing the voice!"

00:03:46.067 --> 00:03:48.133
-It is my voice, yeah.

00:03:48.133 --> 00:03:52.200
I should also mention, by
the way, "Bluey's Big Play" is

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:55.467
a show, a live "Bluey" show
that was just at

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:57.334
Madison Square Garden
that I just missed.

00:03:57.334 --> 00:03:58.434
I'm like, oh, my gosh.

00:03:58.434 --> 00:03:59.534
But I'm sure
it'll come back around.

00:03:59.534 --> 00:04:01.901
But it's a giant phenomenon now,
"Bluey."

00:04:01.901 --> 00:04:04.334
In fact, also it is a balloon

00:04:04.334 --> 00:04:06.000
in the Macy's Thanksgiving Day
Parade.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.667
-Yeah.
-Now, is that a big --

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:08.968
Do you know what that is
in Australia?

00:04:08.968 --> 00:04:12.234
-Well, it was explained to me
from friends in L.A.

00:04:12.234 --> 00:04:15.701
just, like, how monumental
that is.

00:04:15.701 --> 00:04:18.367
Because I was like, "Oh, we have
some float in a parade."

00:04:18.367 --> 00:04:19.801
-Yeah, there's a balloon
somewhere.

00:04:19.801 --> 00:04:21.334
-It's Thanksgiving.
Is it a thing?

00:04:21.334 --> 00:04:22.434
-It's a massive deal.

00:04:22.434 --> 00:04:23.834
-And people are like,
"It's a thing!"

00:04:23.834 --> 00:04:26.501
-It's a massive deal
to have a balloon, yeah.

00:04:26.501 --> 00:04:28.934
You have a Bluey balloon.
That's so cool.

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:30.200
It's going to be unbelievable.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.701
It's going to be --
Congrats on that.

00:04:31.701 --> 00:04:35.868
I'm just so happy that you guys
are here and came on the show.

00:04:35.868 --> 00:04:37.634
I'm the biggest fan of the show.

00:04:37.634 --> 00:04:39.601
I want to see a "Bluey" movie,
by the way.

00:04:39.601 --> 00:04:40.901
-Sure.

00:04:40.901 --> 00:04:41.901
-I'd like to see a "Bluey"
movie.

00:04:41.901 --> 00:04:43.367
-A trilogy.
-A trilogy.

00:04:43.367 --> 00:04:44.901
-Yes. Make a trilogy.

00:04:44.901 --> 00:04:47.400
-The pre-story one.
-Let's start with a trilogy.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.567
Yeah, exactly. Very smart, Dave.

00:04:49.567 --> 00:04:51.634
I want to show everyone a clip
from the show.

00:04:51.634 --> 00:04:54.300
Here are Dave McCormack and
Melanie Zanetti in "Bluey."

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:55.434
Take a look a this.

00:04:55.434 --> 00:04:56.868
-Check it out, Mum.

00:04:56.868 --> 00:05:00.167
-Hey, nice strategy,
balloon girls.

00:05:00.167 --> 00:05:02.501
-I'm a keepie-uppie expert.

00:05:02.501 --> 00:05:04.734
-Yeah. But it's not as fun now.

00:05:04.734 --> 00:05:06.267
Can you make it hard again?

00:05:06.267 --> 00:05:08.701
-Sorry, pickle.
I've got my hands full.

00:05:08.701 --> 00:05:11.501
-♪ Oh, good morning, everybody ♪

00:05:11.501 --> 00:05:13.434
♪ I said good morning,
everyone ♪

00:05:13.434 --> 00:05:15.501
Unh. What up, party people?

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:17.234
-Dad, we're playing
keepie-uppie.

00:05:17.234 --> 00:05:18.734
Can you make it harder?

00:05:18.734 --> 00:05:20.901
-Ah, my newspaper.

00:05:20.901 --> 00:05:22.968
-Dad!
-Bingo, help!

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:26.367
-I can't. I'm a newspaper!
[ Giggles ]

00:05:26.367 --> 00:05:28.100
-Oh, I love it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:29.734
It's such a great show.

00:05:29.734 --> 00:05:31.701
I love it, love it,
love it so much.

00:05:31.701 --> 00:05:34.133
Dave McCormack and
Melanie Zanetti, everybody.

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:38.067
You can watch "Bluey"
on Disney Jr. and Disney+.

00:05:38.067 --> 00:05:42.133
Got to blueylive.com for more
info on "Bluey's Big Play."

